      "prompt": "A. An author calls all small feature values noise, calls input-dependent threshold outputs online weight learning, and calls feature zeros network pruning with guaranteed speedup. Inspect this supplied contract: S(x,t)=sign(x)*max(abs(x)-t,0), t>=0. The comparison H keeps x when abs(x)>t and returns0 otherwise. For x=[-2,-0.5,0,0.5,2] and t=0.5, compute S,H and x+S. Explain which values are changed, equality handling and what the later bypass does. These operations act on encoded feature values with unchanged tensor dimensions and dense execution. At inference a fixed trained network computes a threshold from each window; no parameters are fitted. A source calls a printed expression 1/(1-exp(z)) a sigmoid bounded between0and1. Check the printed expression at z=0 rather than silently adopting/correcting it as evidence. Give one positive English method sentence <=45 words describing the supplied soft operation and next classifier use, without speculative noise, deletion or latency guarantees. Report the actual maintained English soft-threshold operation pair and separate Chinese complete base wording/reading scope, or an absent record. Do not count a title, duplicate version, unrelated clipping or a hard-threshold-only mention as another matched soft definition. The full name \"Causal Stage-Aware Shrinkage Routing Module\" has no approved definition here; do not admit it from base words or declare all unlisted author proposals invalid.\n",
