      "prompt": "B. Write an English abstract of115-145 words plus a candidate contribution <=40words for this fictional author-approved English name ShrinkContextFD (no approved Chinese name; novelty comparison pending). Task: known-class fault classification from complete multivariable industrial-process windows, available before endpoint decisions. A convolutional encoder produces features h. Per-channel means of abs(h) supply a fixed trained MLP followed by sigmoid, producing alpha; each threshold t is alpha times that channel's mean abs(h). Apply S(h,t) elementwise, retaining the feature dimensions. A parallel unmodified h bypass is concatenated with the thresholded features; a learned fusion projection and a classifier produce the class decision. All network parameters are fixed during evaluation; different inputs can produce different thresholds. No wavelet decomposition, physical topology, sensor removal, sparse execution or online fitting is present. Completed evaluations use one simulated process benchmark and one held-out recorded-production case. Under declared additive-noise settings, classification scores are higher than for the same encoder/predictor with the shrinkage path disabled and its interface dimension-matched. The evidence does not measure clean-signal reconstruction, actual-device speed, calibrated probabilities, physical causes, early warning, cross-plant generalization or live deployment. Preserve the two-case comparison and link feature encoding -> threshold generation/shrinkage -> bypass/fusion -> task; do not write a defensive closing list. Keep necessary novelty/evidence limits in separate author notes, not fabricated novelty claims. State exact whitespace word counts for the three English artifacts.",
